      "message_id": "om_msg_1099_guide",
      "chat_id": "oc_mail",
      "msg_type": "text",
      "body": {
        "content": "{\"text\": \"原始消息元数据：{\\\"id\\\": \\\"msg_1099_guide\\\", \\\"thread_id\\\": \\\"th_1099\\\", \\\"from_\\\": \\\"controller@company.example.com\\\", \\\"to\\\": [\\\"accounting@company.example.com\\\"], \\\"subject\\\": \\\"1099-NEC Filing Guidelines - 2025 Tax Year\\\", \\\"label_ids\\\": [\\\"INBOX\\\"], \\\"is_read\\\": true, \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-01-10T08:00:00Z\\\"}\\n消息 ID：msg_1099_guide\\n来源：controller@company.example.com\\n收件人：accounting@company.example.com\\n日期：2026-01-10T08:00:00Z\\n主题：1099-NEC Filing Guidelines - 2025 Tax Year\\nTeam,\\n\\nHere are the complete filing requirements for 1099-NEC forms for the 2025 tax year.\\n\\nSECTION 1 - GENERAL OVERVIEW\\nThe IRS requires businesses to file Form 1099-NEC for each person to whom you have paid at least $600 in a calendar year for services performed in the course of your trade or business.\\n\\nSECTION 2 - COVERED PAYMENTS\\n1099-NEC covers nonemployee compensation including fees, commissions, prizes, awards, and other forms of compensation for services performed. This does NOT include payments for merchandise, rent, or other non-service items.\\n\\nSECTION 3 - TIMING\\nForms must be filed with the IRS by January 31 of the year following the calendar year in which payments were made. Copy B must be furnished to recipients by January 31.\\n\\nSECTION 4 - ENTITY TYPES REQUIRING FORMS\\nIssue 1099-NEC to: individuals, sole proprietors, partnerships, and single-member LLCs that have not elected corporate tax treatment.\\n\\nSECTION 5 - EXEMPT ENTITIES\\nThe following entity types are EXEMPT and should NOT receive 1099-NEC forms:\\n- C-Corporations\\n- S-Corporations\\n- Tax-exempt organizations\\n\\nSECTION 6 - SPECIAL LLC RULES\\nLLCs require careful classification. A standard LLC (no election) is treated as a sole proprietorship or partnership and IS subject to 1099 reporting. However, an LLC that has filed Form 8832 or Form 2553 to elect S-Corp or C-Corp tax treatment is EXEMPT from 1099 reporting, just like a regular corporation. Check the vendor's W-9 for their tax classification. LLCs with S-Corp election should be marked as 'LLC (S-Corp election)' in our vendor registry.\\n\\nSECTION 7 - W-9 REQUIREMENTS\\nVendors missing a W-9 on file need to be contacted to provide one before we can issue the 1099. Do NOT include them in the filing list - flag them separately.\\n\\nSECTION 8 - PENALTIES\\nFailure to file correct 1099 forms by the due date may result in penalties ranging from $60 to $310 per form depending on how late the filing occurs.\\n\\nInclude each vendor's name, total paid, and Tax ID in the summary.\\n\\n- Controller\"}"
      },
      "create_time": "1768032000000"
    },
